 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Depends on the size of the matrix $W$ ($N \times M$) and the solver used. Solving the normal equations $W^T W a = W^T o$ involves matrix multiplication and inversion, which is $O(M^3)$ for direct inversion or $O(M^2 N)$ for iterative solvers, where $N$ is the number of pixels and $M$ is the number of voxels/basis functions [S1].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the matrix $W$ ($N \times M$) and the vectors $o$ and $a$ [S1].
